{"id": "w-sample-001", "task_type": "task2", "prompt_text": "Some people think that city governments should spend more money on public transport rather than building new roads. To what extent do you agree or disagree?", "essay_text": "In many fast-growing cities, traffic congestion has become a daily frustration, and governments must decide where to spend limited transport budgets. While new roads may seem like an obvious solution, I strongly believe that investment in public transport brings far greater long-term benefits.\n\nThe main argument against building more roads is that extra capacity tends to fill up quickly. When a new motorway opens, driving becomes temporarily easier, which encourages more people to buy cars and make journeys they previously avoided. Within a few years, the same bottlenecks return, only on a larger scale. By contrast, a well-planned metro or bus rapid transit line can move tens of thousands of passengers per hour in a fraction of the space that private vehicles require.\n\nPublic transport also addresses problems that roads tend to worsen. Air pollution from vehicle exhaust is a serious health risk in dense urban areas, and electric trains or buses can reduce it considerably. Furthermore, affordable transit gives low-income residents access to jobs and education that might otherwise be out of reach, which makes a city fairer as well as more efficient.\n\nAdmittedly, roads remain necessary for freight, emergency services and people living in areas that rail networks cannot serve. It would therefore be unrealistic to stop all road construction. However, these needs can usually be met by maintaining and upgrading existing roads rather than expanding them.\n\nIn conclusion, although some road investment will always be required, the bulk of public money should go to public transport, because it relieves congestion more permanently, improves public health and widens opportunities for ordinary citizens.", "target_band": 7.5, "source": "human", "band_source": "assumed", "teacher_bands": [{"rater": "A", "overall": 7, "task": 7, "coherence_cohesion": 7, "lexical_resource": 7, "grammatical_range_accuracy": 7}, {"rater": "B", "overall": 7, "task": 7, "coherence_cohesion": 7.5, "lexical_resource": 7, "grammatical_range_accuracy": 6.5}], "notes": "Band trong mẫu là GIẢ ĐỊNH để chạy thử harness, KHÔNG phải band giáo viên. Đề và bài do Allingo tự biên soạn."}
{"id": "w-sample-002", "task_type": "task2", "prompt_text": "More and more young people now work remotely for companies based in other countries. What are the advantages and disadvantages of this trend?", "essay_text": "Nowadays, many young people are working online for a company which is in other country. This trend have some advantages and also some disadvantages, I will discuss both side in this essay.\n\nFirst of all, the biggest advantage is about money. Foreign companies usually pay more higher salary than local company, so young workers can earn a lot and help their family. In addition, they can learn many new skill, for example how to use English in the meeting and how to work with people from different culture. This experience is very useful for their career in the future.\n\nOn the other hand, there are some problems. The time zone is different, so sometimes they must work at night and they feel very tired. Also, working at home alone make people lonely because they don't meet colleague in the office. Some people also worry about contract, because if the company stop the job suddenly, the worker cannot do anything because the law is different in each country.\n\nAnother disadvantage is that local companies lose good workers. When talented young people work for foreign company, the local economy maybe not develop so fast.\n\nIn conclusion, working remotely for foreign companies give young people more money and experience, but it also have problems like tiredness, loneliness and unsafe contract. I think the advantages is more than disadvantages if people can manage their time well.", "target_band": 6.5, "source": "human", "band_source": "assumed", "teacher_bands": [{"rater": "A", "overall": 5.5, "task": 6, "coherence_cohesion": 5.5, "lexical_resource": 5.5, "grammatical_range_accuracy": 5}, {"rater": "B", "overall": 5.5, "task": 5.5, "coherence_cohesion": 5.5, "lexical_resource": 5, "grammatical_range_accuracy": 5}], "notes": "Band trong mẫu là GIẢ ĐỊNH để chạy thử harness, KHÔNG phải band giáo viên. Đề và bài do Allingo tự biên soạn."}
{"id": "w-sample-003", "task_type": "task2", "prompt_text": "Some people believe that schools should teach young people how to manage their personal finances. Others think this is the responsibility of parents. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.", "essay_text": "I agree that schools should teach students how to manage money. Because many young people don't know how to save money and they spend all their money for clothes and phone. If school teach this subject, student will know how to make a plan for their money and they will not have debt when they are adult. Also parents are busy and they don't have time to teach their children about money. But some people think school already have too many subject and students are very stress. I think the school can teach money skill in maths lesson, so it is not a new subject. In conclusion, I think teaching money skills is good idea for students.", "target_band": 5.5, "source": "human", "band_source": "assumed", "teacher_bands": [{"rater": "A", "overall": 4.5, "task": 4, "coherence_cohesion": 5, "lexical_resource": 5, "grammatical_range_accuracy": 4.5}, {"rater": "B", "overall": 4.5, "task": 4.5, "coherence_cohesion": 4.5, "lexical_resource": 5, "grammatical_range_accuracy": 4.5}], "notes": "Band trong mẫu là GIẢ ĐỊNH để chạy thử harness, KHÔNG phải band giáo viên. Đề và bài do Allingo tự biên soạn. Bài cố ý ngắn (< 250 từ) để kiểm tra cờ too_short."}
{"id": "w-sample-004", "task_type": "task1_academic", "prompt_text": "The chart below shows the percentage of average household spending on different categories in Arland in 2005 and 2025. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.", "image_description": "Bar chart, invented data (Allingo practice item). Country: Arland. Share of average household spending, 2005 vs 2025: Food 34% -> 22%; Housing 25% -> 38%; Transport 18% -> 15%; Leisure 9% -> 14%; Other 14% -> 11%.", "essay_text": "The bar chart illustrates how households in Arland divided their spending between different categories in 2005 and 2025.\n\nOverall, the proportion spent on housing and leisure increased, while food and transport took a smaller share of the budget over the twenty-year period.\n\nIn 2005, food was the largest expense, accounting for 34% of household spending. However, this figure fell significantly to 22% in 2025. Transport also decreased slightly, from 18% to 15%.\n\nIn contrast, housing costs rose sharply. In 2005 housing made up a quarter of spending, but by 2025 it had become the biggest category at 38%. Spending on leisure activities also went up, from 9% to 14%, which suggest that people had more money for entertainment.\n\nThe remaining expenses, grouped as other, dropped from 14% to 11%. To sum up, the pattern of spending changed considerably, with housing replacing food as the main cost for families in Arland.", "target_band": 7, "source": "human", "band_source": "assumed", "teacher_bands": [{"rater": "A", "overall": 6.5, "task": 6.5, "coherence_cohesion": 6.5, "lexical_resource": 6, "grammatical_range_accuracy": 6}, {"rater": "B", "overall": 6, "task": 6, "coherence_cohesion": 6.5, "lexical_resource": 6, "grammatical_range_accuracy": 6}], "notes": "Band trong mẫu là GIẢ ĐỊNH để chạy thử harness, KHÔNG phải band giáo viên. Đề và bài do Allingo tự biên soạn. Số liệu biểu đồ là hư cấu."}
{"id": "w-sample-005", "task_type": "task1_general", "prompt_text": "The heating in the flat you rent has stopped working. Write a letter to your landlord. In your letter: describe the problem; explain how it is affecting you; say what you would like the landlord to do.", "essay_text": "Dear Mr Thompson,\n\nI am writing to inform you about a problem with the heating system in my flat. Since last Monday, the radiators in all rooms have been completely cold, and the boiler shows a red warning light that I cannot reset.\n\nThis situation is causing me serious difficulties. The temperature at night has dropped below five degrees, so the flat is extremely cold and I have caught a bad cold. In addition, I work from home three days a week, and it is almost impossible to concentrate when I have to wear a coat at my desk.\n\nI would be grateful if you could arrange for a qualified engineer to inspect and repair the boiler as soon as possible, ideally before the weekend. If the repair is going to take longer, could you please provide a portable electric heater in the meantime?\n\nI look forward to hearing from you soon.\n\nYours sincerely,\nMinh", "target_band": 7.5, "source": "human", "band_source": "assumed", "teacher_bands": [{"rater": "A", "overall": 7, "task": 7, "coherence_cohesion": 7, "lexical_resource": 7, "grammatical_range_accuracy": 7}, {"rater": "B", "overall": 7, "task": 7.5, "coherence_cohesion": 7, "lexical_resource": 7, "grammatical_range_accuracy": 6.5}], "notes": "Band trong mẫu là GIẢ ĐỊNH để chạy thử harness, KHÔNG phải band giáo viên. Đề và bài do Allingo tự biên soạn. Tên trong thư là hư cấu."}
